@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nd67-vn10-nouns`

-- Decree 67/2023/NĐ-CP, Article 12(1), (3), (4), (7), (10), (11) and Article 10(1): the duties
-- of the buyer, the insured, the owner and the insurer after an accident, and the working-day
-- deadlines.
--
-- THE CLOCK OF THE REGULATIVE RULES IN THIS MODULE IS WORKING DAYS ("ngày làm việc"), counted
-- from the anchor each rule names (time 0 of its traces). `WITHIN 3` is three working days.
-- Nothing in the language records the unit: only this comment and the BECAUSE strings say so.
-- Where a calendar date is wanted, the date functions below count working days on a calendar.
-- Fork F14: the decree does not say which days are working days. This encoding takes Saturdays
-- and Sundays as non-working and lets the caller supply every other day off. Fork F22: the day
-- of the anchor is not counted (day 1 is the next working day).
-- Duties the decree gives no period stay without WITHIN: they stand until done, and inventing a
-- period would be writing law (Article 12(1)(a) "ngay", at once, names none).
-- DECREE 220/2026 does not amend any of these clauses: one rule answers for both vintages.

§ `Working days`

@ref Decree 67/2023 Article 12(3)-(4), "ngày làm việc", fork F14
GIVEN cal IS A `A working-day calendar`
      d   IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a working day under` cal d MEANS
        `is weekday` d
    AND NOT (elem d (cal's `days off other than Saturdays and Sundays`))

GIVEN cal IS A `A working-day calendar`
      n   IS A NUMBER
      d   IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`under` cal `the day` n `working days after` d MEANS
    IF   n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE IF   `a working day under` cal `the next day`
         THEN `under` cal `the day` (n MINUS 1) `working days after` `the next day`
         ELSE `under` cal `the day` n           `working days after` `the next day`
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS d PLUS 1

§ `Article 12(1) — the duties of the buyer and the insured when an accident happens`

-- (a) notify the insurer's hotline at once, help the injured, limit the harm, keep the scene;
-- (b) not move, dismantle or repair the property without the insurer's consent, except where
--     that is needed for safety, to limit harm to health, life and property, or on an authority's
--     demand; (c) gather and provide the documents of Article 13 that are theirs to gather;
-- (d) help the insurer verify them. None names a period.
